# below, XGBoost) for every (target, candidate) pair, for every
# crop, for every configuration in the grid below. This is
# comparable in cost to running Step 2 once per grid row. If this
# is too slow, set RUN_XGB <- FALSE below to use LASSO only for
# this sensitivity check (XGBoost is the slower of the two fits).
